This is an aggregate. There is no single licence on the rows: each row's
licence follows its source, and is given per row by the view
`reception_licensed` (data/reception.sqlite), from data/licenses.tsv.

1. PUBLIC DOMAIN — NOT CLAIMED

Public-domain commentary (JFB, Matthew Henry, Barnes, Calvin, the Catena
aurea in the Oxford translation, Wesley's Explanatory Notes) is not
claimed. Rows from JFB, Henry, Barnes and Calvin store locations only.

2. THE COMPILATION — CC BY 4.0

This project's own work — the verse keys and their normalization, the
overlap columns, the ingest and alignment, the RCL normalization, and the
code — is licensed under CC BY 4.0.
Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

3. ROWS UNDER OTHER LICENCES

- glossa-ordinaria: CC BY-NC 4.0 (the in-house English of migne.app).
- catena: CC BY-SA 4.0 (Catena's open-data layer).
- barth-cd: pointers only; the Church Dogmatics is in copyright and no
  words are stored.

These licences do not combine into one adapted dataset (BY-NC and BY-SA
are incompatible). Export them as separate files under their own terms.

